          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "In these two sets of equations, the behaviors of acids as proton donors and bases as proton acceptors are represented in isolation. In reality, all acid–base reactions involve the transfer of protons between acids and bases. For example, consider the acid–base reaction that takes place when ammonia is dissolved in water. A water molecule (functioning as an acid) transfers a proton to an ammonia molecule (functioning as a base), yielding the conjugate base of water, OH"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and the conjugate acid of ammonia, NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "4"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              }
            ],
            "id": "zcygafygh7d93mq",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "f2a9m6garvizzik",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "ai0efm6efx7knx6",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/e5/e5d73f3a6b695ad8c456ac4494ca93a0/conjugate_pair.jpg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "700"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "vwmqy3mi9oppqwq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "uz3o9qrcyvc6qb0",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\require{color}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\underset{\\color[rgb]{1.0, 0.0, 0.0}\\textbf{acid}}{{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)}} {\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}+} {\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1} \\underset{\\color[rgb]{0.0, 0.0, 1.0}\\textbf{base}}{{\\mathrm{NH}}_3(aq)}}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;} {\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\rightleftharpoons}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;} {\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\underset{\\color[rgb]{0.0, 0.0, 1.0} \\textbf{conjugate base}}{\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)}}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}+} {\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\;}{\\color[rgb]{0.1, 0.1, 0.1}\\underset{\\color[rgb]{1.0, 0.0, 0.0} \\textbf{conjugate acid}}{\\mathrm{NH}_4^+(aq)}}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The reaction between a Brønsted-Lowry acid and water is called "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "acid ionization"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A reaction involving the transfer of a proton from an acid to water, yielding hydronium ions and the conjugate base of the acid."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "4047575895",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "457769243",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " reaction. For example, when hydrogen fluoride dissolves in water and ionizes, protons are transferred from hydrogen fluoride molecules to water molecules, yielding hydronium ions and fluoride ions:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "n7mggyfhfgxocwe",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "alt": "Lewis structures representing the reaction between HF and H2O.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "mrmk9o5ild6dqhd",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "pdzerht7anyczbd",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/e4/e4381808102808deef1d1e657ad15a1a/hf%2Bh2o_updated.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "450"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "kmqtjwti8tet5qy",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4z1rx6dmydx0g48",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\require{color}\\underset{\\color[rgb]{1.0, 0.0, 0.0}\\textbf{acid}}{\\mathrm{HF}}\\;+\\;\\underset{\\color[rgb]{0.0, 0.0, 1.0}\\textbf{base}}{{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O}\\;\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\underset{\\color[rgb]{1.0, 0.0, 0.0}\\textbf{acid}}{{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+}\\;+\\underset{\\color[rgb]{0.0, 0.0, 1.0}\\textbf{base}}{\\;\\mathrm F^-}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm F^-\\rbrack}{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HF}\\rbrack}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When we add a base to water, a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "base ionization"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A reaction involving the transfer of a proton from water to a base, yielding hydroxide ions and the conjugate acid of the base."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "128089681",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4081766882",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " reaction occurs in which protons are transferred from water molecules to base molecules. For example, adding pyridine to water yields hydroxide ions and pyridinium ions:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "e7parrh9nuqtc99",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "alt": "Lewis structures representing the reaction between water and pyridine",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ox25b9fes1ciiui",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
